 "title": "Ab0920a and Alternaria brassicicola Pathogenicity Cluster",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Ab0920a, an isolate of Alternaria brassicicola, a pathogenic fungus. Ab0920a has secreted the Bax protein and is sensitive to various fungicides. Alternaria brassicicola causes black spot disease in cruciferous crops and has pathogenicity factors, including A. brassicicola and Koch. The cluster also includes other organisms, such as Nicotiana benthamiana, which has pathogenicity to Alternaria, and Agrobacterium tumefaciens, which mediates transformation in R. toruloides MS7013.",
